is this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence’s, inferred from the call."}]}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Return Value","anchor":"return-value","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A sequence of the upstream’s elements, in order, in arrays of one or more."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The strategy decides when the pending elements are flushed: every so many elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/count(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), every interval"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/time(interval:clock:tolerance:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), on a signal or a unit of work"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), whenever any of several does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy\/either(_:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), or by a rule of your own ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/BatchStrategy","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"). After every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"flush, each strategy starts over. A flush with nothing pending emits nothing; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence never emits an empty array."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the upstream finishes, the pending elements, if any, are emitted as a last array and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the sequence finishes. When the upstream throws, the pending elements are dropped and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence throws the same error. A signal that finishes stops firing while the batches go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on; a signal that throws ends the sequence with its error."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The upstream and the strategy run in tasks of their own, started when iteration begins,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the upstream is read ahead of the consumer, and arrays the consumer hasn’t taken yet"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are buffered. Cancelling the consumer, or dropping its iterator, cancels both. An"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"upstream or signal that ignores cancellation keeps the internal task alive until its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pending "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns, and is not read again after that; the batched sequence itself"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ends at once."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Batching needs iOS 16, Mac Catalyst 16, macOS 13, tvOS 16, watchOS 9 or visionOS 1.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Example","text":"Example","type":"heading"},{"code":["for try await batch in [1, 2, 3, 4].async.batch(strategy: .either(.count(3), .time(interval: .seconds(1), clock: ContinuousClock()))) {","    print(batch) \/\/ Prints [1, 2, 3], then [4]","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"name":"Throws","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any error the upstream or the strategy throws."}]}],"style":"note"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:Sci7Afluents8SendableRzsAB7ElementRpzrlE5batch